          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            By analogy with the concept of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              \-graded monad
            in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{M}, \otimes, I)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endo
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            (whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            on
            = succeed "):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{M}, \otimes, I)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  ([\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{C}], \circ, id_{\mathcal{C}})
                  \\,.
          %p
            This generalizes the concept of a plain
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal
            monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
            Equivalently, an
            = succeed "-grading" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+of+a+monoidal+category"} lax action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping#deloopings_of_higher_categorical_structures"} delooping
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathcal{M} \to Cat
          %p
            Just as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            may be defined in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            (besides the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K =
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} \mathcal{M} \to K
          %p
            A further generalization is to category-valued monads, lax functors from any category to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            (
            %a{:href => "#OrchWadEad"}> OrchWadEad
            ), and then to 2-category-valued monads from any 2-category.
          %p
            Graded monads are also known as
            %strong parametric
            monads. The grading idea may also be applied to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonads"} comonads
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The grading may arise from a monoid
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi M
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M, \otimes, e)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_m
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi n
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{m, n, X}: T_m(T_n X) \to T_{m \otimes n} X
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mi e
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{X}: X \to T_{e} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m, n
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-graded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ×
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N}, \times, 1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_n
                returns lists of length
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                of elements of a set.
            %li
              %p
                In computer science, monads model
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/side+effects"} effects
                and comonads coeffects. Grading can therefore allow further annotation of these. For instance, there are graded versions of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reader+monad"} reader monad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state+monad"} state monad
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writer+comonad"} writer comonad
                (
                %a{:href => "#OrchPet"}> OrchPet
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+modality"} graded modality
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+logic"} bounded linear logic
            %li
              %p
                For graded monads relevant for probability theory see (
                %a{:href => "#Perrone"}> Perrone
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Given the strict action of a monoidal category,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
                on a category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
